.TH SIMRV-LINUX-BUILDER 1 "November 2026" "SimRV 3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
simrv-linux-builder \- build RISC-V Linux images for SimRV
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B simrv-linux-builder
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B simrv-linux-builder
downloads and builds generic RISC-V Linux images using supported root filesystem
backends such as Buildroot and Alpine. It can select upstream versions in an
interactive terminal interface, use saved version pins, and accept custom source
locations and root filesystem overlays. The generated images are intended for
booting in SimRV.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-tui
Open the interactive configuration and version picker.
.TP
.B \-\-arch \fIrv32|rv64\fR
Select the target architecture.
.TP
.B \-\-rootfs \fIalpine|buildroot\fR
Select the root filesystem backend.
.TP
.B \-\-profile \fINAME\fR
Select a supported image profile.
.TP
.B \-\-linux-version \fIVERSION\fR
Choose the Linux kernel version.
.TP
.B \-\-opensbi-version \fIVERSION\fR
Choose the OpenSBI version.
.TP
.B \-\-check-updates
Show newer versions available in the configured source catalog.
.TP
.B \-\-rootfs-overlay \fIDIRECTORY\fR
Add files and symbolic links from a directory to the guest root filesystem.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR simrv (1)
